# adversarial perturbation toolchain (offline). The Python venv and the
# scratch/verification clips stay local; message_adv.wav IS committed so others
# can rebuild the scrambled asset with `node tools/garble.mjs` alone (its
# optimization is not bit-reproducible, so the committed clip is canonical). The
# perturbed clip is plainly intelligible by ear — it is the message — and is kept
# in the repo so the build is reproducible, not as a secret.
tools/adversarial/.venv/
tools/adversarial/__pycache__/
tools/adversarial/message.clean.wav
tools/adversarial/verify_*.wav
